 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A book for «الكتاب» (after Musa's name), geometric for «ولولا كلمة سبقت من ربك» and «ليوفينهم ربك أعمالهم». 112 addresses the Prophet ﷺ: no plate. 113: no fire drawn; As-Sa'di's definition of «الركون» (inclining to the wrongdoer in his wrong) keeps the warning precise. 110:14-18 is not glossed (the tafsirs differ on who doubts and what). As-Sa'di's «يقضي بينهم يوم القيامة» (10:93 wording) is cut. STAGING v4: c1 (110-111): We gave Musa the Book and it was disputed: Musa is not drawn (he is named only as the one given the Book, and neither tafsir places him among those who differed; no plate starts on his name). Al-Muyassar: a group believed in it and others disbelieved, so his people are shown as three believers (light robes) and three men in dark robes in a town by day; a book plate for the Book (110:4-6, after Musa's name), the men in dark robes turn away from it on 110:5 (they differed), the camera stays wide (no close-up on ordinary figures right after Musa's name). Geometric for the word that preceded from your Lord (110:8-13; the judgement that did not come is not drawn). 110:14-18 (in doubt): the tafsirs differ on who doubts, so no group is singled out, the camera stays wide. Geometric for your Lord will pay them in full (111:4-10). c2 (112) stays ambient (mountains, steadfastness): the command to the Prophet himself and those who repented with him; his own conduct is never staged and no believers are shown beside an empty place; params.quiet over all of 112; geometric for He sees what you do (112:9-12). c3 (113) stays ambient (night_sky): do not incline to the wrongdoers, or the Fire will touch you: staging it would act the forbidden inclining or put the believers under the threat of the Fire, so nothing is staged; params.quiet over all of 113; a two-paths plate for inclining or not (113:2-5, gone before the Fire is named), geometric for you have no protectors besides Allah (113:8-14); no fire. Cover: the mountains mood for the path of steadfastness."
 },
